From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:33:19 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] s32x-screen

The 32X gets its own Screen section, listed last and shown only when the
card holds 32X games, with five rows. Shader walks Off and the retro list,
stored in Config/s32x_shader.txt; the in-game Shader row and the shader
shortcut walk the same list. Picture is the Mega Drive's: Stretch by
default following the frame width, then Actual and 4:3, stored as 32x in
Config/picture.txt, and every choice draws the size the Mega Drive one
does. PAL Speed is the 32X's own row in Config/pal_speed.txt, Native by
default: PicoDrive reports 50 fps for a PAL cart and ADR 0071 paces it.

Renderer (Accurate, Good, Fast) and Sound Rate (44 kHz, 22 kHz) are
PicoDrive's two speed options, kept in Config/s32x.txt. Accurate and 44
kHz are the factory choice, PicoDrive's own defaults; the user's choice
becomes the default and applies from the next game. A missing line is
the factory choice and an unknown one is logged and read as it.
